  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Based on the current implementation of the Management interface, the REST API must push datastreams into a temporary file before calling addDatastream or modifyDatastream. If, instead, the Management interface provided a way to pass the stream directly, the file could be stored into the final storage location directly, eliminating the need for an extra store and retrieve step. This would be of great benefit to those needing to do bulk loading activities.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
